in his party, on Saturday meets with the CDU/CSU's 90,000-strong Young Union. In Schleswig-Holstein, 3,000 people are expected at an AfD youth rally. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico sentences killers of US, Australian surfers to 158 years each in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:854c9c05a8e0a321ab5a6ec3c429905b2959848e189253b3e4c7a524b6addc42</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975--d9f256fde01a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three Mexican men were found guilty last week of murdering foreign surfers in 2024. The case had drawn global condemnation, particularly in Australia, where two of the victims were from.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France braces for nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4e63a6dd397081688b0848dec144dce02d807f619c1cbc6b873d8b9a3503907</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-braces-for-nationwide-protests/a-79685584--ba700758ca86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-braces-for-nationwide-protests/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists are taking to French streets to protest high prices and inequality. Authorities say they fear the rallies could turn violent.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: 'Cockroach' party founder Abhijeet Dipke under preventive arrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40641d09edada5268a1819c8d69b6b3d03cd80f510fa2c4493335dcf902dd661</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-founder-abhijeet-dipke-under-preventive-arrest/live-79685143--26f18853b264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cockroach-party-founder-abhijeet-dipke-under-preventive-arrest/live-79685143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP's Abhijeet Dipke is due to appear before a Special Executive Magistrate later in the day. Dipke was detained ahead of a demonstration in New Delhi on Friday. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: California wildfires destroy homes, leave thousands without power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed2dc29f67bbbe31605dca5174b3620f1a1e636ec194f0f38346babcc673163a</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480--49bdc655ff84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Multiple mansions have been engulfed in the fires raging in California while firefighters continue to douse the blaze. Thousands of people have been evacuated and many others are without power.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oregon school shooting: Police praise 'heroism' of those who intervened to stop more killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f343ece869ce223d16c8c34be2e20e63fc0c6ded08a0ec3379f5a494b238628b</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302--68385910c32e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US police have praised the actions of three people who cut short a deadly shooting at a school in the state of Oregon. Three children and a teacher were killed in the attack, carried out by a former pupil at the school.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump puts new Russia sanctions on hold</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b76fa5c8b51955bcc2b6fad54074322c0f6ebd87e7b11ee5dd03a91871d0e87d</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T02:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002--586e2562981b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president cited national interests for his decision to sign a waiver on sanctions Congress voted to place on Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation lowest in nearly 40 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed73a1a16200ec2c642a86c8396f1d589b66edfd646da89f5ba81267e9557465</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T22:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906--24b7e4d329ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest figures show that 3,335 square kilometers of the Amazon rainforest were cleared in the year ending in July, the lowest level since 1988. The drop has been described as an "historic achievement."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284763a133c1d543cb26c45f8ae5ca94c3352fa931c3ca0e42982c4d6921fada</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: US journalist injured by Israeli settlers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0a4f18f18d3860db9082beac93631663b9292d112fd5ba790403d923a6edb4</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181--8e9b6bd6853f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington Post journalist Heidi Levine said she was beaten by Israeli settlers in the occupied West Bank. Reporters Without Borders slammed the attack as "brazen violence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House press secretary Zacharia exiting role after short tenure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b5ca4b0140518e82b53a03d61f5593e8a510e17b9089769eb724e64b6839eb</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341--2f88277a7fd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zacharia, having served only five days in the role, is now the shortest-serving press secretary in White House history. Her departure follows a rocky debut at the podium and controversy surrounding her background.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e468adee355c31b7882d1c4d84e4018960687f578027d2e2b6f385c4d4aea958</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>At summit, EU leaders pledge support for Ukraine's Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52498e1ae42616b1f3bf6168937775742deb9e6c8a0bae0c84f177e1e8f865e6</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-summit-eu-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808--25caad1f3ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-summit-eu-leaders-pledge-support-for-ukraine-s-zelenskyy/a-79678808?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Zelenskyy has received words of encouragement from EU leaders, who pledged support for Ukraine's self-defense against Russia. This comes as winter approaches and the US seems to be withdrawing support.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's Abiy Ahmed appoints interim Tigray government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3739db6d126ee2a27414ddac968ad3ab2f5fead10ab3d236ff53ef2f2cfb6a69</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519--c9a39db6c855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-abiy-ahmed-appoints-interim-tigray-government/a-79683519?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Abiy Ahmed's office said there would be elections held in Tigray within 6 months. The move comes after an escalation in fighting between federal forces and a rebel alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, France agree on deal to support Europe's struggling car industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57decffb753f58dde4e20026b9c2ed976d923b61d5a0e9999de388a61a2c63c0</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595--5e23597ac466.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-france-agree-on-deal-to-support-europe-s-struggling-car-industry/a-79678595?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The two countries said the agreement aimed to safeguard Europe's automotive industry, encouraging development and research. Automakers in Europe have so far struggled to compete with Chinese electric car companies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo recovering from surgery, will deliver Sunday prayer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed7c338dd91a5bc6a514e2cd9f61ad9d2de1819dcd6f944bd35bfc41077f8c23</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-recovering-from-surgery-will-deliver-sunday-prayer/a-79682540--e275bd782fd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-recovering-from-surgery-will-deliver-sunday-prayer/a-79682540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Vatican has said that Pope Leo XIV is recovering from lung surgery. Photos released on Friday showed the pontiff celebrating Mass at Rome's Gemelli Hospital unaided.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German colonialism on agenda in Bundestag debate on Namibia genocide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0d9fdc10b2adc77a3e07e7f855d6e7c11aa7ab7f5ae7944b1bdad3b26a634cf</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388--e473209aeb4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-colonialism-on-agenda-in-bundestag-debate-on-namibia-genocide/a-79682388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties have forced a debate in the Bundestag on the early-20th-century genocide Germany carried out in Namibia. Will this finally spur progress in addressing colonial crimes?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Femicide in Iran: When 'honor' becomes a death sentence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46a3c51a978bf1886dbc7cb4b4e0a7c755ae9e3092a088a7ef8426b2836cfd6f</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:17:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977--41194eafafb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:020a01517e0d5a8bffa4c6af14dcc2e51dd343c29370026e74b39ade2e749b28</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks on strategic Saudi assets threaten Riyadh's regional leadership and economic ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08a278fa62d31ccd527824033fc450fcdd214a06d548050c2d888a7758a6dad5</id><updated>2026-10-17T12:16:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambition/a-79680200--af5776370a6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambitions/a-79680200?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis continue to target Saudi Arabia, Riyadh's vulnerability threatens its claim on regional and religious leadership — as well as its standing as an economic powerhouse.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
